---
description: Every app list/page must show a skeleton while loading and a real empty state — never leftover list lines.
globs: "**/*.{tsx,jsx}"
alwaysApply: true
---

# Loading and empty states

Do not render list chrome (ul, dividers, `li + li` borders, pagination bars) until there are items.

```tsx
// BAD — empty list / leftover lines while fetching
const [items, setItems] = useState([]);
return items.length ? <ul>{...}</ul> : <p>No items.</p>;

// GOOD
if (loading) return <ListSkeleton rows={3} />;
if (!items.length) return <EmptyState>No items yet.</EmptyState>;
return <ul>{items.map(...)}</ul>;
```

- Use `ListSkeleton` + `EmptyState` from `components/ui/ListState.tsx`.
- One skeleton language per page, matching that screen: claim `row`, home `news`, amenity `block`, form/detail `detail`, settings `pref`.
- Never mix a blank shimmer slab with structured rows on the same screen.
- First paint uses `ListSkeleton` (thumb/avatar + text lines + chip/button as the real UI has). `LoadingDots` are only for scroll load-more after data is already on screen.
- Never flash the empty sentence during load.
- Never leave a bordered empty `<ul>` or divider when the list is empty.
- Applies to Operations and Warranty screens.
